course: dictionary
lesson: 15780
title: Tying: fastening or same score
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Tying» is the -ing form of the verb tie. It describes something happening: «I am tying my shoelaces.» The context words tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Most of the time, tying means fastening something with string, rope, laces, or a knot. «She is tying the parcel with string.» The words parcel and string are the clues. Check by swapping in «fastening»: «She is fastening the parcel with string» still makes sense.
explain: In games, tying means having the same score as another player or team. «The two teams are tying at three goals each.» Nobody is ahead, so tying means equal. Swap in «fastening» and it does not make sense, so this is the game meaning. Always check the clues.
fact: «Tying» is the -ing form of the verb tie.
fact: «Tying» means fastening something with string, rope, laces, or a knot.
fact: «Tying» in games means having the same score as another player or team.
fact: A knot is a tight join made by twisting or looping a rope or string; a bow is a loop-shaped knot, like the one on your shoelaces.
fact: Useful phrases: tying shoelaces, tying a knot, tying up, tying a bow.
exercise: «Mia is tying her shoelaces before the race.» What is Mia doing? | Buying new laces | Running very fast | *Fastening her laces | Taking off her shoes
exercise: «The two teams are tying at three goals each.» What does tying mean here? | Are winning by a lot | Are leaving the pitch | Are tied up with rope | *Have the same score
exercise: Scouts practise tying knots at camp. Which word is the -ing form of tie? | practise | scouts | *tying | knots
test: «Dad is tying the boat to the dock with a rope.» What does tying mean here? | Sailing away quickly | *Fastening it with rope | Painting the boat | Getting the same score
test: «Sam and Ali were tying in the spelling test, both with 9 out of 10.» What does tying mean? | *Having the same score | Losing badly | Forgetting the answers | Being in the lead
exam: «Hold the rope steady while I finish tying the knot.» What does tying mean here? | *Making a knot | Throwing the rope | Pulling the rope away | Cutting the rope
